Computer Science Engineering courses (CSE full form) mix computer science (software, algorithms and theory) with Engineering (hardware, design and construction) to solve complex technological problems. As per AICTE, 3,90,245 students are enrolled in BTech CSE course yearly. AICTE says India is one of the largest producers of Engineering graduates in the world and Computer Science Engineering courses are the most employable branch among all specialisations.
For Computer Science Engineering courses, candidates must pass Class 12 with PCM subjects and have good knowledge of Maths and Science. Students wishing to get admission must sit for one of the national, state-level and university-level exams like JEE Main, MHTCET, WBJEE, SRMJEE, LPUNEST, etc.
